<title>SINGAPORE: Sunright 1995/96 net profit rises 54 pct.</title>
<headline>Sunright 1995/96 net profit rises 54 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to July 31, 1996</p>
<p>(millions of Singapore dollars unless specified)</p>
<p>    Net profit			 10.09  vs   6.55</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		4.00  vs   4.00</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (cents)    8.2   vs   5.6</p>
<p>    Turnover			  142.63  vs 106.61</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest   1.02  vs   0.86</p>
<p>    Operating profit		 29.31  vs  18.52</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		2.40  vs   1.41</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortization    14.03  vs   7.20</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	 3.04  vs   1.60</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		   15.92  vs  11.51</p>
<p>    Tax				   4.42  vs   3.63</p>
<p>    Minorities (expense)	    1.40  vs   1.33</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries (gain)	  0.18  vs   1.94</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:		February 5, 1997</p>
<p>    Last day books open:	    January 20, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Sunright Ltd is an electronics company specialising in semi-conductor testing.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
